{"event_type":"review","id":"61956d9226b76e8da536aaec8399c19db6770e48273c909ff98a12962cbac5aa","occurred_at":"2026-11-07T07:33:22Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/41719c153cffc40db444a885a0486293ddf976ca42cdbaac833ac3a95578f3e9","sha256":"41719c153cffc40db444a885a0486293ddf976ca42cdbaac833ac3a95578f3e9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cfcdbc1b817363a1a60d15ed3c5c68f7eae11d91cf0e5a3b24d39087aa88ed6a","sha256":"cfcdbc1b817363a1a60d15ed3c5c68f7eae11d91cf0e5a3b24d39087aa88ed6a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/bebe6924df971fd6ca5854ef040e8136b85aa9fe345c5cb6dd9642ca9477cc1f","sha256":"bebe6924df971fd6ca5854ef040e8136b85aa9fe345c5cb6dd9642ca9477cc1f"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/07921663379e722dd79624921c65a6639d058438c042ebe21cb6a7753f3c1b7a","sha256":"07921663379e722dd79624921c65a6639d058438c042ebe21cb6a7753f3c1b7a"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/edaa8eeb17fc73798fc396e8621311e061a4646aad05ee6e44eb821a494e15fb","sha256":"edaa8eeb17fc73798fc396e8621311e061a4646aad05ee6e44eb821a494e15fb"}],"attempt_id":"11f4004c97d21bd73ca3d15f8d8694e8c25423d2dd48d929d7b32045504f2584:0:1","base":"f86c92108ecc4fbbab768bc014fd10127df885c2","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"95626bc6349480209156786a4c7d4c3c90f68aa7","body":"**Throw `DispatchError('config', …)` instead of a plain `Error` at src/driver/factory.ts:356-357.**\n\nThe factory contract is that a bad request fails before dispatch as a structured `DispatchError('config', …)`. The comments in this file say the same. `errorClassOf` reads `dispatchClass` from that error type. A plain `Error` carries no `dispatchClass`, so a caller that sends `beforeRequest` to a non-`ai-sdk` lane gets an unclassified failure. That caller is any lane resolved from a role binding.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  if (request.beforeRequest !== undefined && lane !== 'ai-sdk')\n-    throw new Error('upload scanning requires the ai-sdk request gate');\n+  if (request.beforeRequest !== undefined && lane !== 'ai-sdk')\n+    throw new DispatchError(\n+      'config',\n+      `driver factory: DriverRequest.beforeRequest requires the 'ai-sdk' lane, but role '${request.role}' resolved to lane '${lane}' — upload scanning cannot be enforced there`,\n+    );\n```\n</details>","id":"c5a363ef6ce632472d676695b28bf374d7f3afc98b3035d901f1684af3892d85","intervals":[],"path":"src/driver/factory.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Throw `DispatchError('config', …)` instead of a plain `Error` at src/driver/factory.ts:356-357."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"95626bc6349480209156786a4c7d4c3c90f68aa7","body":"**Guard `bindingProblems` against non-object role entries at src/driver/factory.ts:259-260.**\n\nThe old code validated only the binding for the resolved role. This helper now scans the whole table at construction. A decoded config such as `{ fixer: null }` makes `Object.entries(byProvider)` throw a raw `TypeError`. The comment on lines 261-264 says decoded config must fail as a structured `'config'` throw. This path now violates that, and it fails even for roles the caller never resolves. Report the malformed entry as a problem instead.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n   for (const [role, byProvider] of Object.entries(bindings ?? {})) {\n+    if (typeof byProvider !== 'object' || byProvider === null) {\n+      problems.push(`bindings for role '${role}' must be an object of provider → lane`);\n+      continue;\n+    }\n     for (const [provider, configured] of Object.entries(byProvider)) {\n```\n</details>","id":"9e05ccbf7aa906a48da012c4acf50b4bf8f9c7a26eebc867f97def2b9d48cf93","intervals":[],"path":"src/driver/factory.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Guard `bindingProblems` against non-object role entries at src/driver/factory.ts:259-260."}],"head":"ca921819c45233234a89a5977582ccc8d93511f5","head_tree":"b4ccd79a879cd59b7eca92377c3b119eff95db28","input_scope":[{"blob":"7bee81d04c8da159f72ba94e7f14a238eed53153","intervals":[[6,7],[18,18],[27,27],[50,77],[89,89],[105,106],[113,117],[143,168],[176,180],[186,188],[190,229],[272,272],[274,278],[280,280],[282,348],[350,369],[371,377],[379,383],[385,389],[393,395],[397,406],[408,429],[439,446],[448,464],[467,472],[474,475],[477,478],[480,488],[490,502],[504,510]],"path":"src/driver/README.md"},{"blob":"95626bc6349480209156786a4c7d4c3c90f68aa7","intervals":[[8,10],[25,31],[42,43],[45,47],[77,78],[85,91],[122,131],[134,139],[148,153],[162,181],[198,198],[209,215],[221,223],[225,238],[249,304],[307,310],[317,318],[324,324],[330,345],[356,357],[362,365],[378,378],[380,380],[383,389],[421,421],[427,428],[430,431],[436,437],[439,440],[442,443],[445,457],[464,506],[513,516],[538,555],[557,557],[561,565],[567,567]],"path":"src/driver/factory.ts"},{"blob":"5520691d3202ecb724debb385b349e540b1a6d15","intervals":[[20,20],[37,37],[102,115],[143,155],[166,166],[225,228],[232,237],[239,258]],"path":"src/driver/schema.ts"},{"blob":"a461fd0f1f1c511412641ee4ef8bbe5513325f92","intervals":[[91,123],[130,154],[189,212],[221,222],[282,282],[320,335],[347,361],[363,392],[432,434],[436,436]],"path":"src/driver/types.ts"}],"job_id":"11f4004c97d21bd73ca3d15f8d8694e8c25423d2dd48d929d7b32045504f2584:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":{"blob":"7adba676aa606b084fc7cf13676928e3ef94cbb3","kind":"blob","mode":"100644","path":"src/driver/README.md"},"merge":"6ad492e9bda60974cb02fdaa23834f11c050aa9c","method":"pre-merge","pre":"e9a3e15cca7355682f79a78311ff9158eaaf74fc","source_path":"src/driver/README.md"},"blob":"7bee81d04c8da159f72ba94e7f14a238eed53153","disposition":"included","mode":"100